AC infusion and megadonor-funded ads give Demuth a path to tighten the race"], "rationale": "Polls since June consistently show Klobuchar ahead by seven to fifteen points, prediction markets price a Democratic win at 93-95%, and she has out-raised Demuth roughly twenty to one in a D+3 state. A Republican-sponsored September poll at just two points and a late $10 million outside infusion for Demuth keep this short of Safe.", "watch": "Whether Demuth's newly funded advertising and the scheduled televised debates close the gap toward the two-point margin shown in the most recent Republican-sponsored survey.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Tim Walz (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Minnesota's governorship is open this year, with Tim Walz retiring and Senator Amy Klobuchar running as the Democratic nominee against Republican candidate Lisa Demuth. The state leans Democratic by about three points, and Klobuchar enters with far greater name recognition and a large financial advantage, having raised roughly $7 million to Demuth's $360,000.\n\nPolling since June has consistently shown Klobuchar ahead, with margins ranging from seven to fifteen points, though a Republican-sponsored September survey showed a two-point race. Outside groups have injected new money for Demuth late in the campaign, including a $10 million committee infusion and megadonor-funded advertising. Independent raters broadly place the race in the Solid or Likely Democratic column, and prediction markets price a Democratic win around 95%. The race remains Klobuchar's to lose, with late spending and debates the main remaining variables.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9683, "margin": 10.03}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9647, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.931, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9507, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9476, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9456, "margin": 9.0}]}